Regression demonstration for the agy turn-end token recordless-abort leak
(fix commit 7a30c2d on fm/agy-adapter-upstream-20260906)

Behavioral test: tests/fm-agy-harness.test.sh ::
  "fm-spawn.sh: a spawn that aborts after minting its turn-end token removes it again"

The test simulates a recordless abort inside the token window: the worktree
pointer directory makes the .fm-agy-turnend write fail immediately after the
registry token and state pointer are minted, before any task record exists.
It then asserts the spawn fails AND leaves no registry token, no state token
pointer, no stranded trust entry, and no damage to the operator's pre-existing
trusted-workspace entries.

--- Run A: bin/fm-spawn.sh at pre-fix merge head 24c4a7e, new test present ---

$ git checkout 24c4a7e -- bin/fm-spawn.sh
$ bash bin/fm-test-run.sh tests/fm-agy-harness.test.sh

ok - fm-spawn.sh: a spawn that aborts after registering trust withdraws it again
not ok - the aborted spawn stranded turn-end registry token(s): fm.xHsQkFKRevoD
FM_TEST_END 2026-09-12T19:03:10Z tests/fm-agy-harness.test.sh exit=1 duration_ms=16611 gate_skip=false
FM_TEST_SUMMARY total=1 failed=1 skipped_gate=0 duration_ms=16651

Result: FAILS before the fix. The simulated abort leaves the registry file
fm.xHsQkFKRevoD behind under $HOME/.gemini/antigravity-cli/fm-turn-end.d —
the leak class reported in review (a stranded token with no supported removal
path, permanently blocking the hook's remove action).

--- Run B: bin/fm-spawn.sh at fixed HEAD 7a30c2d (spawn_abort_cleanup
--- withdraws AGY_TURNTOKEN_MINTED on recordless abort) ---

$ git checkout HEAD -- bin/fm-spawn.sh
$ bash bin/fm-test-run.sh tests/fm-agy-harness.test.sh

ok - fm-spawn.sh: a spawn that aborts after registering trust withdraws it again
ok - fm-spawn.sh: a spawn that aborts after minting its turn-end token removes it again
ok - fm-spawn.sh: an abort after the record is published still withdraws the trust it registered
ok - fm-spawn.sh: an abort withdraws both spellings after the worktree is deleted
FM_TEST_END 2026-09-12T19:02:12Z tests/fm-agy-harness.test.sh exit=0 duration_ms=21454 gate_skip=false
FM_TEST_SUMMARY total=1 failed=0 skipped_gate=0 duration_ms=21495

Result: PASSES after the fix. Registry directory empty after the simulated
abort; state pointer and trust entry also withdrawn; operator trust entries
untouched.

Grok/kimi token handling untouched; fm-agy-turnend-hook remove semantics
untouched, per the accepted scope.
